# Engineer F-SUBMIT build report (CASMI26)

## Status: COMPLETE (code written + verified; heavy compute excluded by brief)

## Files written/edited (all in ~/code/casmi26)
1. src/f_ranker.py  (modified)
   - Added model persistence: fits 8 HistGB (2 priors {0.5,0.6} x 4 seeds), saves
     joblib dict {"rankers": [...], "feat_dim": 20} -> data/franker_model.pkl.
   - Added train_and_persist() for a background runner (fit + persist, no eval pass).
   - Extracted shared core features_for_query(qm,qp,target, rep,nmr, acoff,acmz,acp,aik,
     key2pool,pool_fp,pool_keys,pool_mass, qkey) from query_features; query_features is
     now a thin adapter passing L.coff/L.cmz/L.cp/L.ik (bit-identical output; validation
     split/SEED-11 logic unchanged so MRR ~0.2670 is preserved).
   - main() = _fit_persist() + holdout eval (unchanged metrics loop).

2. src/f_submit.py  (NEW, main deliverable)
   - Loads data/franker_model.pkl (clear error if missing; verifies feat_dim == 20).
   - Builds inchikey14->normalized_smiles map from train.parquet.
   - Builds test Lib keyed by molecule_id via the EXACT analog_accel _clean_all path
     (object.__new__(Lib) so the same cleaning produces cmz/cp/coff).
   - Train analog reps built identically to f_ranker (first finite-nm row per key,
     sorted by neutral mass).
   - For each of 400 unique test molecules: picks first/highest rep spectrum, runs the
     SAME features_for_query against trainpool candidates, 8-rankers mean proba, ranks,
     top-25, maps keys->SMILES, pads to 25 when short. Emits submission.csv and prints
     [F-SUBMIT] wrote submission.csv (400 rows).

